{title: Higher Ground}
{artist: Johnson Oatman Jr. / Charles H. Gabriel}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{tempo: 96}
{time: 4/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 491장}
{title_ko: 저 높은 곳을 향하여}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I'm pressing on the upward way
New [C]heights I'm gaining [G]every day
Still [G]praying as I'm onward bound
Lord, [D]plant my feet on [G]higher ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Lord, lift me up and let me stand
By [C]faith, on Heaven's table [G]land
A [G]higher plane than I have found
Lord, [D]plant my feet on [G]higher ground
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]My heart has no desire to stay
Where [C]doubts arise and fears dis[G]may
Though [G]some may dwell where these abound
My [D]prayer, my aim, is [G]higher ground
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]I want to scale the utmost height
And [C]catch a gleam of glory [G]bright
But [G]still I'll pray till heaven I've found
Lord, [D]lead me on to [G]higher ground
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
